WEBVTT

NOTE
English subtitles for a German-language film. Translated from YouTube's
German auto-transcript of the original, with the speech recogniser's
mangling of the product names corrected — it heard "APRP", "AP+", "Ak"
for APplus, and "Elli", "Ill", "ILI", "Els", "II" for Elly.
Not an official Asseco translation.

1
00:00:01.309 --> 00:00:03.330
[music]

2
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.310
Hello, Elly.

3
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.190
Hello, Kim. How can I help you today?

4
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.030
Could you introduce yourself briefly?

5
00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:22.270
Of course. I'm Elly, your helpful AI assistant,

6
00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:25.390
integrated into the APplus ERP system.

7
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.790
I can help you with questions about APplus, provide information,

8
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.230
and support you in using the system.

9
00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:35.670
If you have questions, I'm here to help.

10
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.710
Great. How does project management work in APplus?

11
00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:43.390
Project management in APplus is a complete solution,

12
00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:45.470
fully integrated with the other APplus modules.

13
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.270
It lets you manage both small and very large projects,

14
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.630
splitting them into several levels or sub-projects.

15
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.470
Work packages and tasks can be assigned under a project.

16
00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.110
Before a quote is drawn up, projects can be planned

17
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.470
for time, cost and the resources they need.

18
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.150
Every cost a project incurs — sales activity,

19
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.150
engineering work — can be recorded.

20
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.230
APplus project management also covers rough and detailed

21
00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:19.750
scheduling of activities, plus special functions like

22
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.470
percentage-of-completion analysis and project risk analysis.

23
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.470
Everyone involved in the project, internal or external,

24
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.790
is fully integrated into the system. They have access to

25
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.430
all the relevant information: contacts, project costs and hours,

26
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.430
documents and much more.

27
00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:45.470
That makes planning, monitoring and managing projects considerably easier.

28
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:50.910
Elly draws on all the information, documentation and training material

29
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.230
in APplus, and makes sense of it for the user.

30
00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.710
The user is guided through every relevant APplus function,

31
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.910
and Elly can explain exactly what APplus is doing.

32
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.830
All of this works not only by talking to Elly —

33
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.270
it works just as well by typing.

34
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:16.000
So let's ask her in the chat how dynamic attributes work in APplus.

35
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.590
Elly doesn't just look up what dynamic attributes do.

36
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:30.230
I can also ask exactly what I have to do to create one.

37
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:36.910
Below the answer she lists links to all the documentation and manuals,

38
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:45.230
so one click takes me straight into the docs — here, for dynamic attributes.

39
00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.670
Now we ask not just how the process works in general,

40
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:56.030
but how a dynamic attribute is actually created in APplus.

41
00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:01.750
Again, Elly walks me through creating the attribute step by step,

42
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.350
and lists the exact explanation and links to every relevant document.

43
00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.950
And Elly isn't only integrated into APplus itself.

44
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.790
She also offers everything you'd expect from general AI features.

45
00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:23.000
So I can ask her, for example, to write a sales text for a packaging machine.

46
00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.310
Elly now uses everything she knows to write that text

47
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.350
for the packaging machine, and I can take it straight back into APplus.

48
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.390
Just as easily, I could have that text translated into another language.

49
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:44.830
So I'll simply ask her to translate it into Polish.

50
00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:49.070
Another considerable time saving. The text is fully translated into Polish,

51
00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.790
and I have my translation for the packaging machine.

52
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.510
With Elly we reach another milestone in APplus product development.

53
00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:02.350
Using state-of-the-art LLM technology together with Flow,

54
00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.470
working with APplus becomes more efficient and more effective.

55
00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.910
That sets a new standard for digital assistance in ERP:

56
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:16.520
more process reliability, guided working, and a forward-looking user experience.
